Package: qdfauction
Type: Package
Title: Nonparametric Quantile Density Estimation and Structural Analysis of First-Price Auctions
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Hassan", "Doosti", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "Hassan.doosti@mq.edu.au",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0290-8122",
                       affiliation = "School of Mathematical and Physical Sciences, Macquarie University")))
Description: Nonparametric estimators of the quantile density function
    (the derivative of the quantile function, also called the sparsity
    function): direct kernel and boundary-corrected kernel smoothers of the
    empirical quantile function, Poisson-weight and Bernstein-polynomial
    smoothers, and indirect estimators via the density (Jones 1992; Soni,
    Dewan and Jain 2012) and via a Poisson-smoothed distribution function
    (Chaubey, Dewan and Li 2024), and linear, hard-thresholded and
    block-thresholded wavelet estimators (Chesneau, Dewan and Doosti 2016;
    Shirazi and Doosti 2022). Smoothing parameters are chosen by biased
    cross-validation, robust likelihood cross-validation (Wu 2019) or a
    weighted biased cross-validation. Later releases apply these estimators
    to the recovery of private values, private-value densities and expected
    revenue in first-price sealed-bid auctions (Doosti, Dewan and Talebian
    2025 <doi:10.1016/j.econlet.2025.112670>; Doosti 2026
    <doi:10.1016/j.econlet.2026.112837>).
